@spec mm_blob_serialise_spec  src=tests/specs/mm_blob_serialise_spec.lua  loc=103  sha=c1de112  cases=5
@exercises midiBlob (midiBlob)
@surface   midiBlob.render, midiBlob.buildWire, midiBlob.parse

# Intent
  Round-trip pin for the write-path codec (inverse of parse).
  
  buildWire + render turn mm-shape records into a MIDI_SetAllEvts blob. The
  contract is parse(render(buildWire(x))) == x -- byte layout may reorder events
  that share a ppq, but the per-type record lists round-trip identically.
  Passthrough carries events parse doesn't model so a whole-take rewrite stays
  lossless.

# Helpers
  @fn ser(notes, ccs, texts, passthrough, endPpq)  @ 15-17
      -- Most cases want bytes out of records, not the wire state in between; name the
      -- composition once so each case reads as the round trip it is testing.
  @fn tailPpq(blob)  @ 50-57
      -- The trailing all-notes-off marker carries the take length (EOT); endPpq
      -- places it past the last event so a whole-take rewrite never shrinks the take.

# Cases
  @case 'records survive serialise -> parse:  ..'  [pure]  @ 23-31
  @case 'unmodelled events round-trip through passthrough'  [pure]  @ 36-45
  @case 'colliding note onsets warn loudly and still serialise'  [pure]  @ 62-78
  @case 'endPpq positions the EOT tail; never shrinks past the last event'  [pure]  @ 82-88
  @case 'render twice over one wire yields identical bytes'  [pure]  @ 94-100

# Uses (outbound edges)
  @use call midiBlob.render  @ 16,99
  @use call midiBlob.buildWire  @ 16,98
  @use call midiBlob.parse  @ 25,27,40,43,76,97

# Fields (r read / w write incl. constructor keys)
  @field r ShowConsoleMsg  @ 69
